&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who Are We?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Postman is the world’s leading API platform, used by more than 45 million+ developers and 500,000 organizations, including 98% of the Fortune 500. Postman is helping developers and professionals across the globe build the API-first world by simplifying each step of the API lifecycle and streamlining collaboration—enabling users to create better APIs, faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is headquartered in San Francisco and has offices in Boston, New York, Austin, Tokyo, London, and Bangalore - where Postman was founded. Postman is privately held, with funding from Battery Ventures, BOND, Coatue, CRV, Insight Partners, and Nexus Venture Partners. Learn more at postman.com or connect with Postman on X via @getpostman.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P.S: We highly recommend reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://api-first-world.com/&quot;&gt;The &quot;API-First World&quot; graphic novel&lt;/a&gt; to understand the bigger picture and our vision at Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;960&quot; data-end=&quot;1267&quot;&gt;The Forward Deployed Engineering (FDE) team tackles some of Postman&#39;s most strategic technical challenges. We partner directly with enterprise customers to solve problems that don&#39;t fit neatly into existing product boundaries, building production-grade solutions that often become core product capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1269&quot; data-end=&quot;1596&quot;&gt;As a Sr. Forward Deployed Engineer, you&#39;ll operate at the intersection of engineering, product, and customer success. You&#39;ll deploy Postman&#39;s critical infrastructure into customer environments, solve complex distributed systems challenges, and build the enterprise foundations that enable customers to safely adopt AI at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1598&quot; data-end=&quot;1815&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This isn&#39;t consulting or professional services. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;re an engineer building production systems alongside customers, turning real-world deployments into durable platform capabilities used by thousands of organizations. &amp;nbsp;This team will build 0-to-1 products from scratch - innovative, strategic initiatives designed to unlock hundreds of millions of dollars in new revenue.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1817&quot; data-end=&quot;1952&quot;&gt;If you enjoy difficult engineering problems, working directly with customers, and building products from the field, you&#39;ll thrive here.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customize and deploy Postman&#39;s data-path components into customer environments and make them run reliably: deployment, hardening, and the field engineering required to operate on infrastructure we don&#39;t control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer for performance, availability, and fault tolerance where it&#39;s hardest: live traffic on the critical path, running in environments we don&#39;t control. Hold the line on latency and reliability under real customer load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the IT controls and enablement that unlock Applied AI for our customers: the identity, policy, governance, and observability that let an enterprise safely run AI agents against their APIs. This is the layer that turns &quot;interesting AI demo&quot; into &quot;AI in production&quot; inside a regulated enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn field experience into a product. Take what you learn in real customer deployments and feed it back to core engineering, hardening one-off solutions into durable product capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the engineering bar for FDE&#39;s data-path work in the field, mentor engineers, and help grow the team as the surface expands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3704&quot; data-end=&quot;3853&quot;&gt;You are an experienced backend or distributed systems engineer who enjoys solving difficult technical problems while working directly with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3855&quot; data-end=&quot;3871&quot;&gt;You likely have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3873&quot; data-end=&quot;4805&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of backend or systems engineering experience, with proven end-to-end ownership of large-scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high-throughput, low-latency backend services, with strong command of concurrency, performance tuning, fault tolerance, and high availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level engineering in a backend or systems language such as Go, Python, Java, Rust, or C++, on Linux, with strong debugging skills in complex production codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record as a technical lead or architect on a significant backend system, setting technical direction and raising the quality bar across a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ownership and ambiguity: able to work autonomously in a small team, make decisions independently, and drive high-stakes projects to completion in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder&#39;s interest in enterprise IT controls and enablement (identity, authorization, policy, governance, observability) as the foundation that lets customers adopt Applied AI safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and a genuine willingness to engage directly with customers and field teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1dtylgm&quot; data-start=&quot;4812&quot; data-end=&quot;4826&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4828&quot; data-end=&quot;4881&quot;&gt;We&#39;re especially excited if you have experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;4883&quot; data-end=&quot;5547&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with software deployed and operated in customer environments (on-prem, appliance, agent, or self-hosted), including install, upgrade, and remote diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with identity and authorization (OAuth2, OIDC, SCIM), API gateways, or policy enforcement systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the agentic AI stack: LLM-based agents, MCP, evaluation frameworks, or agent orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building observability into products deployed across many heterogeneous customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-section-id=&quot;1ny543q&quot; data-start=&quot;5554&quot; data-end=&quot;5581&quot;&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love This Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;5583&quot; data-end=&quot;6071&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;z64rmu&quot; data-start=&quot;5583&quot; data-end=&quot;5670&quot;&gt;Solve technically challenging distributed systems problems with real customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;luskqe&quot; data-start=&quot;5671&quot; data-end=&quot;5782&quot;&gt;Work directly with some of the world&#39;s largest enterprises as they modernize their API and AI infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;net964&quot; data-start=&quot;5783&quot; data-end=&quot;5882&quot;&gt;Influence Postman&#39;s product roadmap by transforming customer problems into platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1qtot4v&quot; data-start=&quot;5883&quot; data-end=&quot;5978&quot;&gt;Help define and build a growing Forward Deployed Engineering organization from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;a0d1fl&quot; data-start=&quot;5979&quot; data-end=&quot;6071&quot;&gt;Build the infrastructure that enables enterprises to safely deploy AI at production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reasonably estimated base salary for this role ranges from $220,000 to $240,000, plus a competitive equity package. Actual compensation is based on the candidate&#39;s skills, qualifications, and experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4036&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;What Else?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;In addition to Postman&#39;s pay-on-performance philosophy, and a flexible schedule working with a fun, collaborative team, Postman offers a comprehensive set of benefits, including full medical coverage, flexible PTO, wellness reimbursement, and a monthly lunch stipend. Along with that, our wellness programs will help you stay in the best of your physical and mental health. Our frequent and fascinating team-building events will keep you connected, while our donation-matching program can support the causes you care about. We’re building a long-term company with an inclusive culture where everyone can be the best version of themselves.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;At Postman we value in person collaboration. We are in office 5 days a week for all roles based out of our hubs in San Francisco Bay Area, Boston, Austin, New York City, Tokyo and London. For roles based in Bangalore, employees currently work in the office three days a week and will transition to five days per week by the end of the year. We were thoughtful in our approach which is based on collaboration and grounded in feedback from our workforce, leadership team, and peers. The benefits of our in office model will be shared knowledge, brainstorming sessions, communication, and building trust in-person that cannot be replicated via zoom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3620&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3633&quot;&gt;At Postman, we create with the same curiosity that we see in our users. We value transparency and honest communication about not only successes, but also failures. In our work, we focus on specific goals that add up to a larger vision. Our inclusive work culture ensures that everyone is valued equally as important pieces of our final product. We are dedicated to delivering the best products we can.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4048&quot;&gt;Postman is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender perception or identity, national origin, age, marital status, protected veteran status, or disability status. Headhunters and recruitment agencies may not submit resumes/CVs through this website or directly to managers. Postman does not accept unsolicited headhunter and agency resumes. Postman will not pay fees to any third-party agency or company that does not have a signed agreement with Postman.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;RDQ427R463&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are passionate about enabling data teams to solve the world’s toughest problems—from making the next mode of transportation a reality to accelerating the development of medical breakthroughs. We do this by building and running the world’s best data and AI infrastructure platform so our customers can use deep data insights to improve their business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Genie One is building the AI coworker for business users: a trusted, governed way to ask questions of enterprise data, explore insights, and take action in the flow of work. Our team brings that experience to users wherever they are—across the web, mobile, and desktop applications—so a field employee, executive, or knowledge worker can move from question to insight without being constrained by a browser or a desk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Software Engineer on the Genie One Mobile &amp;amp; Desktop team, you will define and deliver the technical foundations for this multi-surface experience. You will work at the intersection of Web UI, Mobile, Desktop, shared frontend infrastructure, and enterprise-grade authentication and governance. This is an opportunity to shape a product and an architecture that are still evolving rapidly: deciding what should be shared, what should be platform-specific, and how to keep the whole system coherent as new capabilities arrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The impact you will have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction for Genie One across web, native mobile, and desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of customer-facing experiences on iOS, Android, macOS, and Windows, balancing web feature parity with native capabilities such as notifications, background activity, multi-window workflows, deep links, and local-file interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape and execute the long-term product and engineering strategy for Genie One Mobile &amp;amp; Desktop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable cross-surface primitives, contracts, and patterns with shared product capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the hybrid codebase easier to evolve by improving boundaries between web views, native shells, platform APIs, shared services, authentication, session management, and client-side state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar for quality and operational excellence for Mobile &amp;amp; Desktop: testing, release automation, telemetry, performance, security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multiply team through technical leadership, mentoring, and hands-on contributions to the most important problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we look for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering experience and a track record of shipping and operating customer-facing products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff-level technical leadership: setting direction across teams, making durable architecture decisions, and driving complex projects from definition through adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid product background spanning web UI, mobile, desktop, or shared frontend platforms—with the ability to drive across all of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with JavaScript or TypeScript and modern web frameworks such as React, plus hands-on experience with mobile or desktop application development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to navigate and improve a dynamic codebase spanning shared web code, React Native or native modules, desktop shells, webviews, backend APIs, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building secure, reliable products involving authentication, session management, enterprise networking, permissions, sensitive data, and enterprise device/application management such as Mobile Device Management (MDM) and Mobile Application Management (MAM).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-focused, bias-to-action mindset and excellent communication skills. You make pragmatic trade-offs, learn quickly, and collaborate effectively across engineering, product, design, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be an expert in every framework or operating system. You do need to be comfortable working across layers and keeping interconnected web, mobile, and desktop experiences coherent as the product evolves.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Databricks is committed to fair and equitable compensation practices. The pay range(s) for this role is listed below and represents the expected salary range for non-commissionable roles or on-target earnings for commissionable roles.&amp;nbsp; Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to job-related skills, depth of experience, relevant certifications and training, and specific work location. Based on the factors above, Databricks anticipates utilizing the full width of the range. The total compensation package for this position may also include eligibility for annual performance bonus, equity, and the benefits listed above. For more information regarding which range your location is in visit our page &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.databricks.com/sites/default/files/2024-08/us-pay-zone-mapping.pdf&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Zone 1 Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$261,250 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why User Behavior?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build the backend systems that fundamentally shift how Roblox responds to unsafe behavior - from reactive, stateless punishment to a personalized, adaptive system that reflects who a user actually is.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own core backend infrastructure for a new capability at Roblox: a low-latency behavioral data layer, a centralized rules-and-inference engine, and a unified intervention-delivery framework that together let us treat users based on their real risk profile instead of a single point total. This is a rare opportunity to build foundational, high-scale systems that directly shape how Roblox understands and responds to risk across hundreds of millions of users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will feel a deep sense of responsibility building systems that directly affect millions of users, especially minors, on one of the world&#39;s largest platforms. Your work will reduce harm, improve fairness, and help ensure Roblox remains a place where creativity and community can thrive safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the User Behavior Foundation: &lt;/strong&gt;Design and operate the low-latency, per-user behavioral data layer that powers real-time safety decisions - aggregating signals like violation history, in-game reports, and behavioral patterns into a single queryable source of truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Consequence Engine: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and evolve the centralized decision engine that combines deterministic rules with ML risk signals into a single, consistent safety decision&amp;nbsp; the authoritative system every consequence flows through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Feature Restriction Platform: &lt;/strong&gt;Build a unified, backend-driven framework for delivering safety interventions that any product team can plug into, replacing today&#39;s fragmented, feature-specific implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unify Abuse Reporting: &lt;/strong&gt;Build the backend that consolidates reporting channels into a single, scalable framework - integrating LLM-based classification, agentic review workflows, and ML models to improve report routing, prioritization, and reporter feedback while meeting global regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design for trust and auditability: &lt;/strong&gt;Build serving infrastructure that meets a high bar for explainability and fairness, since these systems directly determine consequences for millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ship code, not just designs: &lt;/strong&gt;Own end-to-end delivery - from system design through migration, testing, and production operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and operating production backend systems at scale, ideally in Go or a comparable statically-typed backend language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience designing distributed systems: service APIs (RPC/gRPC), data modeling for high-throughput event ingestion, caching, and low-latency read paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and evolving rules engines, workflow/decision systems, or similarly stateful business-logic services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with streaming or batch data pipelines feeding a feature store or similar ingestion layer, and comfort partnering with ML engineers who consume that data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid production operations fundamentals: monitoring, alerting, oncall, capacity planning, and incident response for systems with real user-facing impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience in Trust &amp;amp; Safety, fraud, risk, or other adversarial domains; experience with feature stores or ML-serving infrastructure; experience building frontend-agnostic, backend-driven UI frameworks (e.g. server-driven intervention/notification rendering).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Systems Thinker:&lt;/strong&gt; capable of designing infrastructure that other teams (ML, feature teams, policy) build on top of, not just point solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Pragmatic Builder:&lt;/strong&gt; scrappy and impact-oriented, comfortable turning scattered, undocumented signals and legacy code paths into clean, well-owned services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable with Ambiguity:&lt;/strong&gt; this space is actively being redefined — you&#39;ll help set the standard, not just implement one handed to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Reliability-Minded Engineer:&lt;/strong&gt; you treat testing, migrations, and oncall as first-class parts of the job, not afterthoughts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Committed to Ethical, Responsible Engineering:&lt;/strong&gt; dedicated to building systems that are fair, auditable, and operate with the utmost responsibility toward user safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,750&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$243,290 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roblox provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. Roblox also provides reasonable accommodations to candidates with qualifying disabilities or religious beliefs during the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For US based roles only, please note the Company may not be able to employ candidates for this role who have United States work authorization related to certain U.S. visa categories, or support future H-1B sponsorship at this time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
